@* MainLayoutProfile — Auth project variant (the file may be named differently depending on the
   modeled Profile Menu element's name — this is the common "MainLayoutProfile" case).

   SAMPLE ONLY: this file demonstrates the structural layout of an Auth-profile dropdown.

   Menu items must be generated ONLY from the provided context (or from modeled Navigation Target
   End context routed to the Profile region). Do NOT add Login/Register/Manage/Logout unless they
   are present in that context.

   If the context requires auth-based gating, use AuthorizeView around the relevant items. If the
   context does not describe auth items, do not invent them.

   Notes:
   - The outer UserMenu structure shows a common pattern: AccountCircle trigger and a stacked
     list of buttons.
   - The NotAuthorized block is OPTIONAL and should only be included when the context explicitly
     includes signed-out links such as Login/Register.
   - Any logout pattern (e.g. POST form + antiforgery) is app-specific; include it only when
     the context explicitly asks for it.
   - NEVER use a MudIconButton instead of the MudIcon in the trigger, as it will break the layout and styling of the menu.
*@

<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <UserMenu>
            <Trigger>
                <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.AccountCircle" />
            </Trigger>
            <ChildContent>
                <MudStack Spacing="0">
                    <MudButton Href="/my-orders" Variant="Variant.Text" Color="Color.Inherit" FullWidth="true">
                        My Orders
                    </MudButton>
                    <MudButton Href="/account" Variant="Variant.Text" Color="Color.Inherit" FullWidth="true">
                        Account
                    </MudButton>
                </MudStack>
            </ChildContent>
        </UserMenu>
    </Authorized>
</AuthorizeView>

@* Optional structure example for signed-out state.
   Include this ONLY if the context explicitly includes signed-out links (e.g. Login/Register). *@

@* 
<AuthorizeView>
    <NotAuthorized>
        <UserMenu Title="Account">
            <Trigger>
                <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.AccountCircle" />
            </Trigger>
            <ChildContent>
                <MudStack Spacing="0">
                    <MudButton Href="/Account/Login" Variant="Variant.Text" Color="Color.Inherit" FullWidth="true">
                        Login
                    </MudButton>
                </MudStack>
            </ChildContent>
        </UserMenu>
    </NotAuthorized>
</AuthorizeView>
*@
